    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can create personalized learning paths for students by adapting to their pace and mistakes. They can explain concepts in relatable ways, like comparing calculus to baking or physics to knitting. This makes math less intimidating and more engaging for diverse learners."
